    <section id="faq">
      <h2>FAQ</h2>

      <h3>Why does Wander Walls request camera access?</h3>
      <p>Camera access is needed for AR room scanning and wall-based gameplay. The camera feed is used by iOS and AR frameworks to understand the room and place game content.</p>

      <h3>Does Wander Walls upload camera footage or room scans?</h3>
      <p>No. Wander Walls is designed as a local-first game. We do not operate a server that receives your camera feed, room scan, gameplay images, or scene placement data.</p>

      <h3>What happens if I deny camera access?</h3>
      <p>AR scanning and room-based gameplay may not work. You may need to enable camera permission in iOS Settings to play.</p>

      <h3>How are paid packs handled?</h3>
      <p>Paid packs are purchased, verified, and restored through Apple StoreKit and your Apple ID. Wander Walls does not directly process payment card information.</p>

      <h3>Can purchases be restored?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Use Restore Purchases in the app. Restore behavior depends on your Apple account, App Store services, and purchase eligibility.</p>
