      <h3>4. Children and family use</h3>
      <p>Wander Walls may appeal to families and children, but the app is intended for use with appropriate parent or guardian supervision. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13 or the minimum age required by applicable law. If you believe a child provided personal information to us, contact us and we will take reasonable steps to address the request.</p>

      <h3>5. Room scanning and private spaces</h3>
      <p>Because AR gameplay uses the device camera, you should avoid scanning sensitive documents, private screens, personal records, or other information you do not want visible on your device. Wander Walls does not intentionally collect or upload room images, but you are responsible for choosing safe and appropriate play spaces.</p>

      <h3>6. Data retention and deletion</h3>
      <p>Local gameplay data remains on your device until you reset it in the app if available, clear related app data through iOS behavior, or delete the app. Deleting the app removes local app data from that device, subject to Apple backup and restore behavior. Purchase records are managed by Apple and may remain associated with your Apple ID according to Apple policies.</p>

      <h3>7. Your rights</h3>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, or a copy of personal information we control. Because Wander Walls does not operate an account system or upload gameplay data to our servers, many requests may relate only to information you provide when contacting support. Contact us using the address above and include enough information for us to process and verify your request.</p>

      <h3>8. Security</h3>
      <p>We use reasonable safeguards appropriate for a local-first mobile game, but no method of storage, transmission, or processing is guaranteed to be 100% secure. Device security, passcodes, operating system updates, and Apple account protections are important parts of protecting your data.</p>

      <h3>9. Policy updates</h3>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make changes, we will revise the effective date above.</p>
